&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mission Brief&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Manager Quality Assurance &amp;amp; Quality Engineering, you are accountable for translating the company quality strategy into effective governance, measurable objectives, and consistent execution across the organization. You will provide independent quality leadership, ensure customer and certification requirements are embedded into business processes, and maintain clear visibility of organizational quality performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is not limited to maintaining procedures or reacting to non-conformances. It is about building a prevention-focused quality system, strengthening engineering and operational decision-making, and ensuring the organization remains ready for customer, regulatory, and certification scrutiny as products and production scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your Role in Our Space Mission:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement and continuously develop the company quality strategy in alignment with business, product, and operational priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the Quality Assurance and Quality Engineering function, establishing clear ownership, priorities, standards, and development plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define, deploy, and monitor quality objectives, KPIs, and improvement targets across the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and facilitate management reviews, ensuring quality performance, risks, trends, and required decisions are clearly presented and followed through.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own customer quality governance, including quality requirements, customer interfaces, escalations, reporting, and the coordination of customer quality reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the primary quality interface to certification bodies and coordinate certification, surveillance, and recertification activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish quality planning and assurance approaches for products, projects, processes, and organizational changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide Quality Engineering leadership for risk prevention, including FMEA, control plans, process capability, measurement strategy, and verification planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Govern non-conformance, corrective action, and preventive action processes, ensuring root causes are addressed and actions are effective.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive cross-functional resolution of systemic quality issues and ensure lessons learned are translated into standards and preventive controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor organizational quality performance and provide transparent reporting to senior leadership on compliance, customer quality, product quality, and improvement priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product Assurance, Supplier Quality, Production, Engineering, and the Chief Quality Inspector organization to ensure clear interfaces and end-to-end quality governance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualification Checklist&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s or Master&#39;s degree in Engineering, Quality Management, Manufacturing, or a related technical discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience in Quality Assurance, Quality Engineering, Product Quality, or Quality Management within aerospace, space, defence, automotive, or another highly regulated engineering environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven leadership experience managing quality teams and influencing cross-functional organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of EN 9100 / AS9100, ISO 9001, and risk-based quality management principles; familiarity with ECSS requirements is advantageous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with customers, certification bodies, auditors, and senior management on quality performance and compliance topics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical knowledge of quality planning, FMEA, control plans, process capability, root cause analysis, corrective action, and structured problem-solving methods.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience defining quality objectives, management review inputs, KPIs, and organizational quality performance reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to balance independent assurance with pragmatic support for engineering and manufacturing execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong stakeholder management skills with the confidence to challenge decisions, escalate risks, and drive accountability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, concise communication and professional proficiency in English; German language skills are advantageous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Aim high, deliver relentlessly, act with integrity, and keep the mission first.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
